WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:06.440
English actor, comedian, screenwriter, producer
and notorious prankster Sacha Baron Cohen

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:09.260
is known for pushing the envelope with his
original characters.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:15.000
From British suburban rapper Ali G to Kazakhstani
journalist Borat, Cohen's antics have established

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.379
him as a household name.

00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:20.700
But we haven't heard much from the controversial
actor lately, which makes us wonder: why won't

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.680
Hollywood cast Sacha Baron Cohen anymore?

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.140
Retired characters

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:30.210
Aside from a promotional appearance on Jimmy
Kimmel Live in 2015, Borat hasn't shown up

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.810
much since 2008.

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:36.220
Austrian fashion reporter Brüno and Admiral
General Aladeen have all but disappeared as

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:37.220
well.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:41.640
The humor of Cohen's films came from fooling
unsuspecting victims, which is almost impossible

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.030
to accomplish these days.

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:46.020
"And then we all laugh, high five."

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:47.020
(laughs)

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:49.540
In an interview with the Daily Mail, Cohen
explained:

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:54.580
"Every new person who sees the movie is one
less person I can be Borat or Bruno with again,

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:56.989
so finishing a movie means having to say goodbye."

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:59.469
Ali G still shows up every so often, though.

00:00:59.469 --> 00:01:02.920
Most recently, he was a presenter at the 2016
Academy Awards.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:06.810
Cohen explained that the Academy wanted him
to present as himself, so he had to sneak

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:07.810
his costume in.

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:12.009
"But my thing was I knew that they would be
trying to see if I would smuggle anything

00:01:12.009 --> 00:01:17.580
in, so my wife very kindly smuggled the beard
in her underwear."

00:01:18.869 --> 00:01:19.860
Too risky

00:01:19.869 --> 00:01:22.860
Cohen's brand of humor is, admittedly, not
for everyone.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:27.909
For an episode of Da Ali G Show, he dressed
up as Borat and lead an antisemitic sing-along

00:01:27.909 --> 00:01:29.759
in a bar in Arizona.

00:01:29.759 --> 00:01:32.609
Cohen received a number of complaints about
the incident.

00:01:32.609 --> 00:01:35.020
The Anti-Defamation League even wrote to him,
saying:

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:38.710
"We are concerned that the irony may have
been lost on some of your audience.

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:42.450
[…] In attempting to expose bigotry and
prejudice you also bear a responsibility to

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:43.450
be sensitive."

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:46.679
But society has changed since Borat hit theaters
in 2006.

00:01:46.679 --> 00:01:51.469
"We support your war of terror."

00:01:51.469 --> 00:01:54.749
In an interview with The Telegraph, Cohen
admitted that he didn't think his films would

00:01:54.749 --> 00:01:59.279
get made if he pitched them today, as studios
would rather make a profit than take a risk.

00:01:59.279 --> 00:02:01.239
Disruptive and destructive

00:02:01.239 --> 00:02:06.939
In September 2008, Cohen, as flamboyant fashion
reporter Brüno, crashed Milan fashion week.

00:02:06.939 --> 00:02:11.770
He used fake passes to get backstage at an
Agatha Ruiz de la Prada show, and wore a suit

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:13.350
made entirely of velcro.

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:17.580
He even managed to get onto the catwalk, which
he strutted down with a variety of costumes

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:19.140
stuck to his body.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:23.220
Eventually, the lights went out, he was removed
by security, and had to explain himself to

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:24.470
the Italian police.

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:28.420
A spokeswoman for the National Chamber of
Italian Fashion told The Telegraph that while

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:29.880
Cohen's stunt gave her a good laugh,

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:31.890
"Some people were very angry and annoyed."

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:36.470
However, many of Cohen's victims have moved
past anger and into lawsuits.

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:40.040
In an interview with Today, Cohen joked that
he thinks he holds the Guinness World Record

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:41.970
for most sued actor in history.

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:46.190
The executive director of Desert Valley Charities
tried to sue the Bruno crew, claiming that

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:48.930
one of Cohen's pranks left her confined to
a wheelchair.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:53.370
A Palestinian grocer who was portrayed in
Bruno as a terrorist settled a slander suit

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:56.610
against both Cohen and David Letterman for
defamation of character.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:01.500
Two South Carolina college students, a Baltimore
driving instructor, a Macedonian singer and

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:05.440
the Romanian village of Glod have all tried
to sue the man behind Borat.

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:06.560
"Mmmm…"

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:11.620
Borat also ended up offending the entire country
of Kazakhstan with its backwards and bigoted

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:12.620
portrayal.

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:17.020
But former deputy foreign minister Rakhat
Aliyev seems to have realized that all publicity

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:21.050
is good publicity, as he invited Cohen to
Kazakhstan, saying that he wanted to show

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:22.050
Borat that:

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:26.190
"Women drive cars, wine is made of grapes,
and Jews are free to go to synagogues."

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:27.319
Too offensive

00:03:27.319 --> 00:03:31.510
While one might assume Cohen isn't concerned
with political correctness, that's far from

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:32.510
the truth.

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:36.040
"This is our Mexican chair people.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:38.850
Demi Moore have two of them in her house.

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:39.850
Sit here."

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:44.510
If you can even believe it, plenty of his
jokes have ended up on the cutting room floor.

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:46.440
"9-11, it's the best."

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:52.440
(speaking foreign language)

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:56.520
Cohen told The Telegraph that he and his writers
will always stop to discuss whether they're

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:58.459
going too far with any of their jokes, saying:

00:03:58.459 --> 00:04:00.900
"There are a lot of jokes that I would not
make.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:03.250
[…] I am continually filtering stuff that
is too much."

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:07.100
But today, as society has become more inclined
to speak out against the offensive and the

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:10.050
insensitive, Cohen's job has only become more
difficult.

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:11.060
He says:

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:13.130
"Comedy is a weird thing that's hard to analyse.

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:15.170
I work very hard to make these films.

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:17.609
[...] I want the movie to be as good as possible.

00:04:17.609 --> 00:04:20.310
[…] Sometimes they work and sometimes they
don't."

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:21.310
He bailed on Queen

00:04:21.310 --> 00:04:26.979
In 2013, Cohen was set to play Freddie Mercury
in an official bio-pic sanctioned by the surviving

00:04:26.979 --> 00:04:28.669
members of the band Queen.

00:04:28.669 --> 00:04:31.509
But when creative differences arose, Cohen
called it quits.

00:04:31.509 --> 00:04:35.460
In an interview with Howard Stern, Cohen talked
about Queen's lead guitarist, who was also

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.520
the lead producer of the film, saying:

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:41.270
"Brian May is an amazing musician, but he's
not a great movie producer."

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:43.099
"They are a band.

00:04:43.099 --> 00:04:45.259
They want to protect their legacy as a band.

00:04:45.259 --> 00:04:47.830
They wanted it to be about Queen, and I fully
understand."

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:50.600
In an interview of own, May was less polite,
saying:

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:54.650
"We had some nice times with Sacha kicking
around ideas, but he went off and told untruths

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:55.729
about what happened.

00:04:55.729 --> 00:04:58.409
[...] It's obvious that it wasn't going to
work, him playing Freddie.

00:04:58.409 --> 00:05:00.349
It wouldn't suspend your disbelief."

00:05:00.349 --> 00:05:01.710
Diminishing returns

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:06.240
Since Cohen's breakout hit, Borat, each of
his subsequent films made less money than

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:07.419
the one before.

00:05:07.419 --> 00:05:11.710
His latest film, The Brothers Grimsby, was
a flop, with an opening weekend gross of only

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:13.780
$3.2 million.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:16.720
Sony's former distribution chief Rory Bruer
told Variety:

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:18.479
"We certainly wanted more.

00:05:18.479 --> 00:05:22.189
Sacha is amazing and we love him, and we tried
to crack the code on it, but it just didn't

00:05:22.189 --> 00:05:23.310
happen for us."

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:25.979
However, Cohen is still developing his own
films.

00:05:25.979 --> 00:05:30.779
In 2016, he was attached to an American remake
of Klown, a Danish comedy, as well as a film

00:05:30.779 --> 00:05:34.110
adaptation of the classic comic strip Mandrake
the Magician.

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:37.539
Will he really be able to work his magic and
get back in the spotlight?

00:05:37.539 --> 00:05:38.539
Time will tell.

00:05:38.539 --> 00:05:39.539
